{"op": "merge", "keep": {"id": "a4ff642f-28f8-416b-9ee3-338909612357", "name": "PUBLIX SUPER MARKETS, INC."}, "lose": [{"id": "bee013b7-2c1c-4dff-9036-a7259a41db23", "name": "PUBLIX SUPERMARKETS, INC"}, {"id": "2912f496-66f3-41ab-9325-f40a64be9f20", "name": "Publix"}, {"id": "e5527267-4cbf-4d18-979d-145d7f62052c", "name": "PUBLIX SUPERMARKET INC"}, {"id": "8b0b7729-53fa-4e3f-b5d9-6850c255231e", "name": "PUBLIX COMPANIES"}, {"id": "22cdfc07-b0dd-4501-bb9a-f19f2c5b4545", "name": "PUBLIX INC."}, {"id": "f2fed1f3-7121-439a-8ff0-6e4fa6f0345b", "name": "Publix Super Market"}, {"id": "5560aa23-2b63-4e96-af9d-fc2854e39b1c", "name": "PUBLIXSUPER MARKETS, INC"}], "date": "2026-09-04", "note": "Seven spellings of the Publix corporation as a political donor — $1.81M of corporate checks split off from the $13.65M on the canonical node — folded onto PUBLIX SUPER MARKETS, INC. (re-kinded organization the same day). All seven were already organization. The store-level payees ('PUBLIX #1140', 'Publix Nocatee', …) are vendor receipts with no giving and are left as they are."}
{"op": "manual-sql", "file": "migrations/manual/publix-committee-fields.sql", "applied": "2026-09-04", "note": "Companion to the Publix set-kind: clears the committee_type ('ECO') and status ('closed') that came with the misclassification, to the organization convention (NULL, unknown). kindLabel prefers committee_type, so the panel was still calling the corporation an Electioneering Comm. Org."}
{"op": "manual-sql", "file": "migrations/manual/drop-interest-and-cfr.sql", "applied": "2026-09-05", "note": "The graph is only for real PAC and candidate money. Drops interest income (INT and its county truncation IN, plus penny rows described as interest), 'transfer to interest bearing account' expenditures (treasury parking; a bank deposit is never filed at all), and every row on CHRISTIAN FINANCIAL RESOURCES, the 501(c)(3) church loan fund the Jones committees used as a savings account, whose redemptions were filed as checks and read as a $1.1M original source. Run on every database, then rebuild. The same rules now run at ingest."}
