{"op": "merge", "keep": {"id": "5de46fe3-122f-41cf-bc06-3a0f8f7a24e2", "name": "Empower Parents PAC"}, "lose": [{"id": "ce133cde-77a7-4a79-b064-660a576da129", "name": "FRIENDS OF RON DESANTIS"}], "date": "2026-09-06", "note": "One committee under two names: state account 70275, registered as Friends of Ron DeSantis and renamed Empower Parents PAC in 2023 (the registry now returns nothing for the old name, and the detail page for 70275 gives chair Blaise Ingoglia and treasurer Nancy H. Watkins). The state relabelled the committee's own filings, so its $186.8M of receipts sits under the new name, but recipients had already written the old one on their reports and the contribution feed built a second node from those: $95.3M given, $85.9M of it to the Republican Party of Florida. Splitting the two made the committee look like it raised nine figures and spent $47k. Keeping the registered name; the old spelling survives as an alias. The merge puts both filings of the same 2023 payments to the state party on one pair, which is what lets collapseMirrors see them; the $3M refund of 2023-02-08 is filed by both sides as an expenditure and needs migrations/manual/desantis-refund-mirror.sql, which collapseMirrors cannot reach."}
{"op": "manual-sql", "file": "migrations/manual/desantis-refund-mirror.sql", "applied": "2026-09-06", "note": "Companion to the Empower Parents / Friends of Ron DeSantis merge: the $3M the Republican Party of Florida refunded on 2023-02-08 is filed by both sides, and once the two names are one node it counts twice in opposite directions. Both rows are expenditures on opposite from/to pairs, so collapseMirrors cannot match them. Drops the party's copy and keeps the committee's own negative REF line, which nets against the gross gift on the same pair. Run on every database, then rebuild."}
{"op": "manual-sql", "file": "migrations/manual/drop-placeholder-officers.sql", "applied": "2026-09-06", "note": "A committee with no chair, treasurer or agent files a word rather than an empty cell, and the detail page prints that word where a name goes. Read as a person it became an officer named \"None\" on 231 committees, plus three \"No Chairman Designated\" rows the bulk extract had already supplied: a hub in registration links and a line in the panel, made out of a blank. 238 rows dropped. isOfficerPlaceholder in normalize.ts now drops them at ingest. committee_officers ships wholesale in sync-to-vps.sh, so this does not need running on the VPS."}
{"op": "merge", "keep": {"id": "067553e5-33d7-4b6f-88b1-ee8fe8e1fd0c", "name": "UNITED STATES SUGAR CORPORATION"}, "lose": [{"id": "39faa7ca-7555-471d-a66d-0b7bc7f2c02e", "name": "US SUGAR"}, {"id": "b89a1a3e-af32-4413-b86a-f84bdf050fda", "name": "US SUGAR CORPORATION"}, {"id": "3f470b76-8580-40e0-8e37-4865554e1f60", "name": "U.S. SUGAR CORP."}, {"id": "f9d07873-15ab-4797-80e6-aec771a4fb4d", "name": "UNITED STATE SUGAR CORPORATIONS"}, {"id": "6d38bd37-f38c-4b9c-bb02-5a109c145fe5", "name": "US SUGAR CORPORTION"}, {"id": "b085a02b-f828-4838-ae6d-01b31d33e99f", "name": "UNITED STATES SUGAR COOPERATION"}, {"id": "887cdb2c-ea3f-43bc-9512-2275d9efbeaa", "name": "US SUGER CORP"}], "date": "2026-09-06", "note": "Eight spellings of the sugar producer at Clewiston, folded onto its registered name: US SUGAR ($6.71M), US SUGAR CORPORATION ($326k), U.S. SUGAR CORP. ($303k), UNITED STATE SUGAR CORPORATIONS ($10k), US SUGAR CORPORTION ($5k), UNITED STATES SUGAR COOPERATION ($1k, and kinded individual), US SUGER CORP ($1k). All eight file from CLEWISTON, FL and give only; none has an expenditure row, none pays another, and no recipient filed the same gift under two spellings, so the merge adds 687 contribution rows and creates no duplicate. Together $21,136,479 against the $13.78M the largest spelling showed alone. Name matching had already found most of these — the keeper carries thirteen review aliases including 'US SUGAR CORPORATION' at 0.717 — but they scored under the 0.88 gate, which is what left them as separate nodes. Industry stays 'Sugar' from NAME_OVERRIDES on the surviving name, rather than the generic 'Agriculture' the misspellings fell through to. Not merged: the Belle Glade and Loxahatchee sugar growers, which are other companies, and 'Alliance of Florida's Sugar Farmers', a registered committee. Also unmerged, and a separate judgement: the US Sugar subsidiaries filing from the same town — South Central Florida Express, Southern Gardens Groves, Southern Gardens Citrus Holding and Citrus Nursery, $762,525 between them."}
{"op": "drop-alias", "entity": {"id": "6b93c7e5-8fe8-4f38-9f10-4c9c728e18fc", "name": "SUGAR"}, "alias": "U.S. SUGAR CORP.", "date": "2026-09-06", "note": "A $1,000 donor called SUGAR in Costa Mesa, California had picked up 'U.S. SUGAR CORP.' as a 0.62 review alias on the strength of the word alone. Below the 0.88 gate, so lookup ignored it, but it points a Clewiston spelling at the wrong company and the merge above makes it wronger."}
{"op": "merge", "keep": {"id": "9232ec31-238f-4331-b913-e153a44a077b", "name": "SUGAR CANE GROWERS COOPERATIVE"}, "lose": [{"id": "8a033a41-d46a-4880-8d03-3882452c0a73", "name": "SUGAR CANE GROWERS CORPORATION"}, {"id": "291b665e-e8d9-4ab6-880a-cb5e88417c9c", "name": "SUGARCANE GROWERS CO-OP"}, {"id": "d08044bb-5791-4340-9568-41d32a2684b2", "name": "SUGAR CANE GROWERS CO-OP OF FLORIDA"}, {"id": "4ce68f2f-2112-4fbe-9754-d3700857a17e", "name": "SUGARCANE GROWERS COOPERATIVE"}, {"id": "1a904e72-b898-4cf0-b9de-e0adf42bf2bb", "name": "SUGAR CANE CO-OP"}], "date": "2026-09-06", "note": "Six spellings of Sugar Cane Growers Cooperative of Florida, the Belle Glade grower-owned sugar mill, folded onto one node: SUGAR CANE GROWERS CORPORATION ($5,000), SUGARCANE GROWERS CO-OP ($3,000), SUGAR CANE GROWERS CO-OP OF FLORIDA ($3,000), SUGARCANE GROWERS COOPERATIVE ($2,000, kinded individual), SUGAR CANE CO-OP ($500). $233,400 across 118 filings against the $219,900 the largest spelling showed alone. Every row is a contribution it made; none of the six has an expenditure row, none pays another, and no recipient filed the same gift twice, so the merge adds no duplicate. The keeper is the spelling 84 of the filings use; the full legal name survives as an alias. Not the same as Sugarcane Raw Bar Grill in Las Vegas, and not the same as the other growers at Loxahatchee, Okeechobee and Clewiston."}
{"op": "set-kind", "entity": {"id": "9232ec31-238f-4331-b913-e153a44a077b", "name": "SUGAR CANE GROWERS COOPERATIVE"}, "kind": "organization", "date": "2026-09-06", "note": "A grower-owned sugar mill, not a political committee. It has no registration with the Division of Elections, no committee type, receives nothing and gives $233,400, and not one of its 118 filings carries a (PAC) tag. Kinded committee it was traversable, so the funding trace walked through it as a conduit and looked for donors behind a corporation that has none. The re-kind also re-derives the industry, which the name override now answers with Sugar."}
{"op": "alias", "entity": {"id": "067553e5-33d7-4b6f-88b1-ee8fe8e1fd0c", "name": "UNITED STATES SUGAR CORPORATION"}, "alias": "US SUGAR CORPORATION", "date": "2026-09-06", "note": "Merged away today, but the survivor already carried this spelling as a review alias scored under the 0.88 lookup gate, and the merge deferred to it rather than raising it. Ignored at lookup, the spelling would build a fresh node on the next ingest and undo the merge. Pinned at full confidence. mergeEntities now raises the loser's own name on conflict, so a later merge does not repeat this."}
