{"op": "manual-sql", "file": "migrations/manual/sugar-industry.sql", "applied": "2026-09-06", "note": "Labels the remaining Florida sugar producers Sugar rather than the generic Agriculture: New Hope Sugar Company and Sugar Farms Co-op at Loxahatchee, Deep South Sugar Corp at Okeechobee, Pioneer Ranch & Sugar Farms at Belle Glade, Sugar Daddy Cane at LaBelle. Sugar was already its own label for Florida Crystals and US Sugar; the rest of the industry sat with cattle ranches. The label has to be per company — every sugar producer files its occupation as AGRICULTURE or FARMING, and a name rule on 'sugar' would catch a liquor store, a preschool and three mobile home parks. NAME_OVERRIDES now names each, so a database built from scratch gets it right; this fixes the rows already loaded, which backfill-industry will not touch because it only fills NULLs. Run on every database."}
