{"op": "merge", "keep": {"id": "fb5dbdf3-a4ea-46e6-b44b-c11727698bbe", "name": "Conservatives"}, "lose": [{"id": "c26fc84b-ebc6-4758-a4a2-ea456e159dda", "name": "CONSERVATIVE LEADERSHIP COMMITTEE, INC (DBA CONSERVATIVES)"}], "date": "2026-09-08", "note": "State account 65559, under its legal name. The loser is ten filed spellings of Conservative Leadership Committee, Inc., four of which write the DBA into the name, and it held $5,586,591 across 99 rows with no registration record of its own. The state's own filings prove the identity from both sides: 79 of those 99 rows, worth $5,482,091, are the counterparty half of a row the registered committee filed itself — same partner, same date, same amount, opposite direction. Florida Trust reported $12,000 in from CONSERVATIVE LEADERSHIP COMMITTEE, INC (DBA CONSERVATIVES) on 2023-03-15 and Conservatives (PAC) reported $12,000 out to FLORIDA TRUST the same day; the pattern repeats across Florida Forward, Florida Courage, Vote Differently, Libertatem and seventeen more, matching row for row and dollar for dollar. Keyed apart, that money is in the graph twice. No money passes between the two records, so the merge makes no self-loop, and collapseMirrors will drop the duplicated half on the next rebuild. The remaining 20 rows, $104,500, are giving the registered record does not carry. This was the single largest dead end in the funding-origins trace. The revoked ECO at the same Tallahassee address, account 59915, is a separate registration holding no money and stays separate."}
