{"op": "merge", "keep": {"id": "d8656201-3d7b-41a9-a632-0f00556176a6", "name": "Realtors Political Advocacy Committee"}, "lose": [{"id": "4cf294a2-d214-4e39-85d1-222479afd033", "name": "Realtors Pol Advocacy Comm"}, {"id": "57f07d5f-a4d0-454b-b667-459cea3de41d", "name": "REALTORS POLITICAL ADVOCACY COMM FL"}, {"id": "c066651b-0722-44eb-9a6c-08d315e0239c", "name": "Realtors Political Advcy. Comm"}, {"id": "126bc6f0-8303-45e0-afc0-0dde0f3a1216", "name": "Realtors Pol Adv Com"}, {"id": "c8047a69-3eec-4e9b-b29f-0891d94676ee", "name": "Realtors Pol Advocacy Cmte"}, {"id": "2e20af8a-b6bf-4868-b529-2fd747ca2d73", "name": "REALTORS POLITICAL ADVOCATY COMMITEE"}, {"id": "c71ec88a-afc0-4e96-9f20-07c9fb801c39", "name": "Realtors Political AdvocacyCom"}, {"id": "5d4ad0fc-811d-434b-b6c2-a51833a39c93", "name": "Realtors Poolitical Advocacy"}, {"id": "81821cc2-43d6-4066-8d28-f7206a59e73c", "name": "REALTORS PC"}], "date": "2026-09-15", "note": "Florida Realtors runs three separate active state committees out of one office at 7025 Augusta National Drive, Orlando: Political Advocacy (account 60584), Political Activity (61237) and Political Action (61239). All three are current registrations, so they stay apart. What folds in here are the names filers typed by hand for them, almost all from the Duval and St. Johns county feeds, where a contributor name is free text. Eight of these are plain misspellings of Advocacy. The ninth, 'REALTORS PC', is the bare string 'REALTORS PAC' that 45 filings use, and it is the one judgement call in this set. It reads as Advocacy on volume and on dates: Advocacy gave $26.1M against $1.0M and $2.3M for the other two, and it is the only one of the three with any filings at all before 2019, which covers the ten REALTORS PAC rows from 2014 to 2018. Four rows resist that reading. Jim Overton (2018-09-17), Ana Maria Rodriguez (2021-11-09) and Rachel Plakon (2022-10-12) each report a $1,000 check from REALTORS PAC and a second $1,000 check from Advocacy under its full name on the same day, which one committee could not lawfully write at the $1,000 legislative cap. Tom Fabricio (2020-09-23) does the same against Political Action. Those four are $4,000 of $105,350 and are left folded in rather than split out."}
