{"op": "split-rows", "from": {"id": "d8656201-3d7b-41a9-a632-0f00556176a6", "name": "Realtors Political Advocacy Committee"}, "where": {"raw": "REALTORS PAC"}, "to": {"id": "83ec0ea7-62c7-452a-ae72-c14d24407569", "name": "Realtors PAC - Florida"}, "date": "2026-09-16", "note": "The bare \"Realtors PAC\" family belongs to state account 4636, not to Political Advocacy. The registry marks 4636 closed and types it a Committee of Continuous Existence, but filers never stopped writing the name and the account carries filings from 2017 to 2026, including $212,000 in 2022. Most of the family already resolves there: \"REALTORS PAC FLORIDA\" at $277,000, \"FLORIDA REALTORS PAC\", \"Realtors PAC Florida\" and \"Realtors PAC Florida-Orlando\". Two Duval reports settle that it is not Advocacy. Lakesha Burton reports $1,000 each from \"Realtors PAC Florida-Orlando\", \"Realtors PAC Florida-Tallahass\" and \"Realtors Political Advocacy Co\" on 2022-10-11, and three checks to one county candidate on one day cannot come from one committee at the $1,000 cap. This reverses the one judgement call in the 2026-09-15 merge. The node then called \"REALTORS PC\" held 45 filings worth $102,000 under this spelling, plus one $850 receipt from Lori Boyer, and it was folded onto Advocacy on volume and on dates. The volume argument was read off Advocacy alone and missed that account 4636 is the larger home for this spelling. Three of those filings also sat beside an Advocacy check to the same candidate on the same day, which was recorded at the time as the reading's cost; moving them here settles all three."}
