{"op": "set-kind", "entity": {"id": "21d89dbb-bbec-4215-8a86-0109b96cdae6", "name": "RUTHERFORD VICTORY FUND"}, "kind": "committee", "date": "2026-09-16", "note": "His own joint fundraising committee, FEC id C00741413, kinded organization because the FEC row carries no entity type and the name reads as a fund rather than a committee. It moved $276,181 into the campaign across 43 transfers, every one of them typed TRANSFER IN AFFILIATED, which is a committee-to-committee movement and nothing else. That is 5.5% of everything the campaign has raised, and as an organization it was a dead end. A joint fundraising committee raises under one banner and splits the proceeds among the campaigns that signed the agreement, so the money has an upstream and the node has to be traversable for anyone to reach it. This is the same call made on TEAM FINE on 2026-09-09."}
{"op": "set-kind", "entity": {"id": "4e21685d-ef54-40e0-8e4e-1ce11934b949", "name": "AIPAC PAC CONDUIT ACCOUNT"}, "kind": "committee", "date": "2026-09-16", "note": "A conduit account, which is a committee that forwards earmarked contributions without taking ownership of them. Eight rows worth $12,000, all in the 2022 cycle. The word account in the name read as a bank account to the classifier and the node was kinded organization."}
{"op": "set-kind", "entity": {"id": "d6f39d29-b8f7-47d6-b2b8-605f1bf82e97", "name": "NFIB SAFE TRUST"}, "kind": "committee", "date": "2026-09-16", "note": "The National Federation of Independent Business's federal PAC, which files under the name SAFE Trust. One row worth $2,500 in 2016. The word trust read as a financial vehicle and the node was kinded organization."}
{"op": "set-kind", "entity": {"id": "4610f8c3-32a2-48a2-9b8f-9c35d8d5b93c", "name": "Seafarers Political Activity D"}, "kind": "committee", "date": "2026-09-16", "note": "The Seafarers International Union's political fund, held under the name a county portal cut at 30 characters. Two federal rows worth $2,000 and one Duval row worth $500. A union's political fund is a committee wherever it files."}
{"op": "set-kind", "entity": {"id": "b3bae73e-3d9f-40f5-a80a-41e2508a5aee", "name": "SCALISE FOR CONGRESS"}, "kind": "committee", "date": "2026-09-16", "note": "Steve Scalise's principal campaign committee. Three rows worth $6,000 here, and two more worth $4,000 in the Fine load. A campaign committee gives to another campaign out of what it has raised, so this node has an upstream and must be traversable to show it."}
{"op": "set-kind", "entity": {"id": "00c47d5c-1647-432c-bb81-d38da658f9b2", "name": "RYAN FOR CONGRESS, INC."}, "kind": "committee", "date": "2026-09-16", "note": "Paul Ryan's principal campaign committee. Two rows worth $4,000. Kinded organization because the name ends in Inc., which the classifier reads as a company."}
