{"op":"merge","keep":{"id":"7396588e-1cb7-4e3a-9c78-7a5c7022cdf9","name":"Florida House Republican Campaign Committee"},"lose":[{"id":"bec3b076-ca73-4f34-887a-86cca03711e6","name":"FHRCC"},{"id":"010b4f48-0a75-4858-b93c-327d5f8fe541","name":"FLORIDA HOUSE REPUBLICANS"},{"id":"6f6b9592-12c0-4083-8941-2cbdaf292153","name":"FLORIDA REPUBLICAN CAMPAIGN COMMISSION"},{"id":"98eb3066-8c4b-4f7b-9b54-89153fe48fe0","name":"FLORIDA HOUSE REPUB. CAMPAIGN COMM."}],"date":"2026-09-18","note":"Account 74084 (PAP, active, Tallahassee, chaired by Sam Garrison with Noreen Fenner as treasurer) plus four unregistered nodes carrying spellings of its own name. \"FHRCC\": the committee's initialism, 2 rows worth $50,156.82, 2021-11-29 to 2025-02-13. Account 74084 already carries the alias \"FLORIDA HOUSE REPUBLICAN CAMPAIGN FHRCC\", which is the same initialism written beside the full name. \"FLORIDA HOUSE REPUBLICANS\": 1 row worth $10,000.00 on 2024-08-23, the committee named by its members rather than its title. \"FLORIDA REPUBLICAN CAMPAIGN COMMISSION\": 1 row worth $5,000.00 on 2024-06-24. Settled by the payer's own ledger: Florida Cow PAC filed that $5,000 as an expenditure to this spelling on 2024-06-24, and account 74084 filed the matching $5,000 receipt from FLORIDA COW PAC on 2024-07-01. One transfer recorded from both ends, seven days apart. \"FLORIDA HOUSE REPUB. CAMPAIGN COMM.\": 1 row worth $112.68 on 2021-05-12, the full name with both words cut short. Twenty-seven further spellings already resolve to 74084 as aliases without ever becoming nodes, which is the same fault stopping one step earlier. No losing node holds a registration, an account number or an officer. Reviewed by hand on 2026-09-18."}
{"op":"merge","keep":{"id":"58ab0474-6b52-40bf-8522-93597b79b9d4","name":"Republican Party of Florida"},"lose":[{"id":"615b29cc-9945-496d-9203-6f5d738bbfc5","name":"REP. HOUSE CAMPAIGNS"}],"date":"2026-09-18","note":"Account 4700 (PTY, active, Tallahassee) plus one unregistered node carrying the filed spelling \"REP. HOUSE CAMPAIGNS\", which is 1 row worth $3,000.00 on 2022-12-16. The party's House campaigns account, filed under a name the party does not use for itself. Settled by the payer's own ledger: Jeff Holcomb booked a $3,000 expenditure to \"REP. HOUSE CAMPAIGNS\" on 2022-12-16, and the Republican Party of Florida booked the matching $3,000 receipt from \"JEFF HOLCOMB CAMPAIGN ACCOUNT\" on 2022-12-15. Same payer node, same amount, one day apart, and no $3,000 reached account 74084 anywhere near that date. \"REP.\" is Republican rather than Representative, and the money went to the party. The losing node holds no registration, no account number and no officer. Reviewed by hand on 2026-09-18."}
{"op": "merge", "keep": {"id": "4e3e130a-c82d-4dc1-af7e-59eaf30b10bc", "name": "REPUBLICAN PARTY OF FLA HOUSE MAJORITY"}, "lose": [{"id": "551226ba-a869-48c8-a41e-2f385913b854", "name": "HOUSE MAJORITY"}, {"id": "0ddd1a9e-7f60-4351-8299-7534a24e11f5", "name": "HOUSE REPUBLICAN MAJORITY"}, {"id": "212a832f-f558-4c04-b827-27408d47d1b8", "name": "REPUBLICIAN PARY OF FL-HOUSE MAJORITY"}, {"id": "8de32f0d-221e-4096-ac2b-0ced0c5c165f", "name": "RPOF HOUSE MAJORITY"}, {"id": "187e3835-d45f-42eb-a9f6-a2af82428150", "name": "FLORIDA REPUBLICAN PARTY - HOUSE MAJORITY"}, {"id": "585ff990-45ff-41d9-89ca-6d831cb90671", "name": "REBULICAN PARTY OF FLORIDA - HOUSE MAJORITY"}, {"id": "34b4f9bf-ab96-494b-a598-ed9dd62873f8", "name": "FLORIDA HOUSE MAJORITY OFFICE"}, {"id": "0eeee5bc-c78a-451c-8628-096df613598a", "name": "HOUSE REPUBLICAN PARTY"}, {"id": "5ce7d331-fbcc-4698-9a25-8e6fb2fb031e", "name": "REPUBLICAN PART OF FLORIDA-HOUSE MAJORITY"}], "date": "2026-09-18", "note": "Ten nodes carry a name for the Republican Party of Florida's House campaign committee, and none of them holds a registration, an account number or an officer. The state's committee list does not carry this committee at all, so there is no registered node to keep and the best-named of the ten is kept instead. It is a separate committee from the party: account 4700 is the Republican Party of Florida and this is not it. The ten hold 66 rows worth $1,358,008.00 between them, and the kept node holds 7 of those. \"HOUSE MAJORITY\": 34 row(s), $935,000.00. \"HOUSE REPUBLICAN MAJORITY\": 8 row(s), $49,000.00. \"REPUBLICIAN PARY OF FL-HOUSE MAJORITY\": 1 row(s), $5,000.00. \"RPOF HOUSE MAJORITY\": 5 row(s), $149,008.00. \"FLORIDA REPUBLICAN PARTY - HOUSE MAJORITY\": 4 row(s), $50,000.00. \"REBULICAN PARTY OF FLORIDA - HOUSE MAJORITY\": 1 row(s), $5,000.00. \"FLORIDA HOUSE MAJORITY OFFICE\": 1 row(s), $5,000.00. \"HOUSE REPUBLICAN PARTY\": 2 row(s), $25,000.00. \"REPUBLICAN PART OF FLORIDA-HOUSE MAJORITY\": 3 row(s), $60,000.00. Spellings rather than committees: a party abbreviated to RPOF or to FLA, a word order reversed, REBULICAN and REPUBLICIAN and PARY typed as they were typed, and an office name used for the committee that works out of it. A hand-run migration moved 47 of these rows onto the party itself on 2026-09-18. That move was wrong and migrations/manual/restore-house-majority-rows.sql undid it, so every row is counted here. Reviewed by hand on 2026-09-18."}
{"op": "rename", "entity": {"id": "4e3e130a-c82d-4dc1-af7e-59eaf30b10bc", "name": "REPUBLICAN PARTY OF FLA HOUSE MAJORITY"}, "name": "Republican Party of Florida House Majority", "date": "2026-09-18", "note": "The kept node's name is a filer's abbreviation, FLA for Florida. Written out, so the committee reads as itself on the site rather than as one filer's shorthand. The nine folded spellings stay as aliases, so a later sweep filing any of them still lands here."}
{"op": "manual-sql", "file": "migrations/manual/restore-house-majority-rows.sql", "applied": "2026-09-18", "note": "Undoes repoint-house-majority-to-rpof.sql, which is kept commented out as the record of it. That migration moved 47 rows onto the party on a test that matched a payer, an amount and a date window. A control set later put that test's false-positive rate at 4.5 percent, so it was never evidence on its own. The rebuild after it read 46 of the moved rows as duplicates of the party's own receipts and deleted them, at a cost of $874,875. This file reinserts the 46 from the production dump of 2026-09-18, returns the 47th, and clears the 46 tombstones."}
{"op": "manual-sql", "file": "migrations/manual/file-house-majority-by-payee-address.sql", "applied": "2026-09-18", "note": "On a Florida expenditure row the address columns describe the payee, not the filer. 112 rows name a House Majority that Florida has never registered: it holds no registration, no account number, no chair, no treasurer, and it has never spent a dollar. 88 of the 112 give the payee's address as 420 East Jefferson Street, where the Republican Party of Florida is the only registrant in the state file. This moves the 49 of those that sat on the standalone node onto the party; the other 39 were already there. It also moves 4 rows given as 527 East Park Avenue onto the Florida House Republican Campaign Committee, account 74084, whose registered address that is. 20 rows stay on the standalone node or the party: 11 give the Florida Capitol room 322, which is the House Majority Office and cannot hold a registration, and 9 give addresses that identify nobody."}
